WHERE THIS COMES FROM
---------------------

Lumen Studio is built on the work of two earlier projects, both MIT licensed:

* godox-ul60bi-bt, the Python library and CLI that first spoke the Godox
  Bluetooth Mesh protocol: provisioning, keys, encryption and the vendor
  command set.
  https://github.com/mattharrison/godox-ul60bi-bt

* ha-godox-mesh, Simon Cheng's Home Assistant fork, which extended that
  library from one light to the whole Godox mesh range and generated the
  per-model capability and gel tables.
  https://github.com/binary-person/ha-godox-mesh

What is used from them:

* packages/godox-mesh-bt/ is the library from ha-godox-mesh v0.2.8. The
  first commit of this repository holds it unmodified; later commits show
  every change made here.
* src/lumen_studio/data/models.json and gels.json are that project's
  generated capability and gel tables (capabilities_data.json and
  color_chips_data.json), copied unchanged.
* src/lumen_studio/data/gel-colours.json is the gel swatch list that project
  fetched from Godox's public colour API (reverse-artifacts/color-chips.json).

The web studio, the real-time engine, the effects, the sync pipeline and the
launcher are new in this repository.

